 "overview": "The Community Preservation Committee (CPC) is responsible for recommending the allocation of Community Preservation Act (CPA) funds toward open space, recreation, historic preservation, and affordable housing projects in Medford. Since its inaugural meetings in 2018, the committee has managed millions of dollars in local surcharges and state matching funds, developing rigorous application guidelines and project evaluation criteria. The body serves as a central hub for reviewing proposals from city departments, non-profits, and private historic property owners. As of October 2026, the committee is reviewing a new round of applications for the 2027 fiscal year while refining its strategies for long-term bonding and large-scale municipal projects.",
