   "name": "Affordable Housing Initiatives",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Early work focused on individual unit construction and heating conversions for housing authority residents. The committee eventually transitioned to multi-year, multi-million dollar commitments for large redevelopments, most notably recommending $2.4 million for the Walkling Court project. Recent work includes the establishment of a dedicated Affordable Housing Trust Fund to manage seed money and homebuyer assistance programs. The committee also supports homelessness prevention through rental assistance grants.",
