   "name": "Brooks Estate Restoration",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Restoration of the historic Shepherd Brooks Manor and its surrounding estate has been a core thread since the committee's inception. Funded projects range from invasive species management and trail restoration to major structural work on the manor's east entryways and wood trim. The committee has also supported professional engineering for the estate's historic 1,900-foot access drive. Most recently, the committee approved a small grant for an archaeological sensitivity report covering the estate and a neighboring cemetery parcel.",
