   "name": "Municipal Building and Infrastructure Maintenance",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "Municipal preservation has increasingly focused on City Hall, including restroom ADA compliance and historically accurate window restorations in the City Council chambers. The committee has also funded repairs for the Condon Shell and studied potential uses for the Curtis Tufts school and the Hegner Center. In 2026, the committee began reviewing a large request for City Hall limestone facade repairs. While it supports municipal assets, the committee denied a pivot request to use preservation funds for fire station HVAC systems, as the work did not meet eligibility requirements.",
