   "name": "Private Property and Religious Institution Preservation",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The committee provides grants for historic preservation on non-municipal properties, including several local churches and sites like the Royall House and Isaac Hall House. Projects often include exterior siding, wood trim restoration, and stained-glass window repairs at Shiloh Baptist and Unitarian Universalist churches. These grants are typically conditioned on preservation restrictions and the exclusion of religious imagery from funded elements. Recent deliberations have focused on establishing stricter guidelines for public funding of private property to ensure functional community use.",
